{"id":"weder","lemma":"weder","pos":"conj","rank":857,"glosses":["neither (only with noch)"],"ipa":"/ˈveːdər/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/De-weder.ogg/De-weder.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Ich habe weder Zeit noch Geld.","en":"I have neither time nor money.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"},null,{"g":"time"},{"g":"still / yet"},{"g":"money"}]},{"text":"Sie kann weder lesen noch schreiben.","en":"She can't write or read.","words":[{"g":"she / they / you"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"},null,{"g":"to read"},{"g":"still / yet"},{"g":"to write, to write out"}]},{"text":"Es ist weder gut noch schlecht.","en":"It's neither good nor bad.","words":[{"g":"it"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},null,{"g":"good"},{"g":"still / yet"},{"g":"bad"}]},{"text":"Ich mag weder Tee noch Kaffee.","en":"I don't like tea or coffee.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to like","l":"mögen"},null,{"g":"tea"},{"g":"still / yet"},{"g":"coffee"}]},{"text":"Weder kann ich, noch will ich gehen.","en":"I can't go, nor do I want to.","words":[null,{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"still / yet"},{"g":"to want","l":"wollen"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"to go, to walk"}]}]}